#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sami-said: print what Sami typed into omp sessions in a time window, oldest first, newest last.

    sami-said [--since 90m] [--until TIME] [--session ID]... [--grep REGEX] [--max-chars N]
              [--json] [--dispatch] [--dispatch-user EMAIL] [--agent-dir DIR]...

--since and --until take a duration back from now (45s, 90m, 2h, 1d) or an ISO 8601 time
(2026-10-28T02:00Z, '2026-10-28 02:00', 2026-10-28), UTC when it names no zone. --since defaults
to 24h, --until to now; --since is inclusive, --until exclusive. --session keeps the sessions whose
id starts with it (repeatable). --grep keeps messages whose text matches it, case-insensitive.
--max-chars cuts each text to N characters. --json prints one JSON object per line instead of text.

Each message carries its UTC time, its source, the session id, the session title, the session's
working directory, and the text. Sources:

  terminal          typed in the omp terminal, and found in omp's prompt history (history.db)
  terminal-history  typed in the omp terminal, in the prompt history, with no copy in a transcript
                    (a /btw question, a slash command such as /guided-goal, or a prompt pulled
                    back before it was sent). Its time is the last time that exact text was sent.
                    A prompt whose transcript copy lands up to 30 minutes after --until counts as
                    sent, and shows in the window that holds that copy.
  dispatch-turn     a person typed it on Dispatch's Agents page and it reached the session as the
                    user's own turn. With --dispatch its author is checked against Dispatch.
  DISPATCH ...      with --dispatch: an answer, comment, message, approval or change request that
                    --dispatch-user (default sami@theorem.dev) wrote in Dispatch, read from the
                    Dispatch event log. These are not in any transcript as typed text.

How a typed message is told apart from text injected into the user role. Structural rules first:

  1. Top-level session files (sessions/<cwd>/<time>_<id>.jsonl) are read. A file below one
     (sessions/<cwd>/<time>_<id>/...) is a subagent transcript of briefs and relays, and is read
     only when the prompt history names its session id for the window: a subagent or lane someone
     typed into. Dispatch messages to such a session show only with --dispatch.
  2. Only entries of type "message" whose message.role is "user" are candidates, plus one custom
     type below. That drops every custom_message (Envoy deliveries, IRC from agents, background-job
     results, compaction and post-compaction reminders, stream goals, rules refresh, LSP and mount
     notices, Dispatch ask reminders, ...), every "compaction" and "branch_summary" entry, and
     every "developer" message (slash-command expansions such as /guided-goal, the "Continue."
     notice the c shortcut sends, advisor and file-mention notes).
  3. message.attribution "agent" is dropped: a parent's brief, an IRC relay, a compaction handoff.
     message.synthetic true is dropped: an automatic continue.
  4. message.tag present: the Dispatch message id of a person's typed input, delivered by Envoy
     (pi-envoy runTypedInput). Kept as dispatch-turn; no further check.
  5. custom_message "skill-prompt" with attribution "user": the user ran /skill:NAME ARGS. Kept
     as the text "/skill:NAME ARGS" from details.name and details.args; the skill body is dropped.
     A tag on the entry makes it a dispatch-turn, as in rule 4.
  6. Every other candidate must match a prompt in the same omp agent directory's history.db, which
     the omp terminal writes on each submit and headless runs (omp -p, RPC prompts from scripts and
     agents) never write. That drops the launch prompts of scripted sessions: reviewers,
     architects, audits, drift checkers, model probes. Match: equal after collapsing whitespace,
     else (same session) one text contains the other and the shorter is 20 or more characters.
  7. A steering message (message.steering, typed while the agent was running) is kept as typed:
     omp stores the text unwrapped, and adds its emphasis wrapper only when it builds a request.
  8. A pruned text "[shaken ~N tokens — recover: artifact://N (region R)]" is restored from the
     session's artifact directory before rule 6, as omp-session-render does.
  9. Agents type into another session's pane with tmux, and the terminal records that as typing. A
     typing call is a bash or eval tool call, in any session file on this machine (nested and
     symlinked ones included), whose arguments say send-keys, paste-buffer or load-buffer (also
     through a helper: tm("send-keys", ...)), or that runs a script (.sh, .bash, .py, or a file in a
     bin/ or scripts/ directory) whose text says so. Its text is its arguments plus every file of
     256 KB or less that it names, read as the file is now: the script, or a brief it sends with
     send-keys -l "$(cat FILE)". A terminal or terminal-history text is dropped when a typing call
     of another session, from 30 minutes before it to 30 seconds after, holds: its first 48
     letters and digits; or half of its 32-character pieces taken every 16 (a template with its
     variables filled in); or, for a text under 16 letters and digits, the whole text as one quoted
     argument. The transcript store (tq) is not used: it cuts a call's arguments at 4000 characters.

Text rules, used only where no structural mark exists:

  T1. A script that types into a pane leaves no tool call (the drift checker's run.sh, the box
      monitor), and a file a call names can have changed since. Agents and scripts name themselves
      on the first line, so a terminal text whose first line matches one of these is dropped:
        ^\\[?From the <up to 100 characters>:<space>   ("From the chief of staff: ...",
                                                     "From the coach, from the audit (...): ...")
        ^\\[(From )?Claude\\b                          ("[From Claude, the ENVOY session ...]")
        ^<CAPS lane tag> here (session <hex>|, at      ("SWITCH here (session 01a174f7). ...")
        ^<CAPS lane tag>, HH:MMZ\\b                    ("CHIEF, 03:09Z: you have been restarted ...")
  T2. A terminal-history prompt is dropped when a terminal message of the same session, within 15
      minutes, starts with its first 60 characters or contains it whole (20 characters or more):
      a draft, or a piece, of a message that was then sent.

Known limits: omp files text typed into a focused subagent view under the parent's session id, so
such text prints as terminal-history of the parent session. Rule 9 misses an agent that types
through a helper defined in an earlier call when the later call never says send-keys, and a script
that was changed or deleted after it sent its text.

Speed: a session file whose mtime is before --since is never opened; in a file over 1 MB a
binary search on byte offsets (probing only "message" entries, which omp stamps as it writes
them) skips to 30 minutes before --since, and reading stops 30 minutes after --until.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import sqlite3
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone
from pathlib import Path

UTC = timezone.utc
DEFAULT_SINCE = "24h"
DEFAULT_DISPATCH_USER = "sami@theorem.dev"
DEFAULT_DISPATCH_URL = "http://localhost:8766"  # the dispatch CLI's default (envoy-client dispatch-config.ts)
SEEK_MARGIN = timedelta(minutes=30)  # omp appends some entries minutes after their timestamp
SEEK_MIN_BYTES = 1 << 20  # files smaller than this are read whole
DRAFT_WINDOW = timedelta(minutes=15)  # rule T2
DRAFT_PREFIX = 60
FALLBACK_MIN = 20  # rule 6, containment match
SSE_IDLE_S = 3.0  # the Dispatch event stream sends nothing more once it has caught up
SSE_TAIL_S = 1.0  # the same wait once the stream has passed the newest event known at the start
DISPATCH_MARGIN = timedelta(minutes=10)
TYPED_BEFORE = timedelta(minutes=30)  # rule 9: how long before a message an agent's send-keys call can be
TYPED_AFTER = timedelta(seconds=30)  # ... and after it, for clock and write skew
TYPING_TOOLS = ("bash", "eval")
TYPED_KEY = 48  # rule 9: letters and digits of a message's start that must appear in the call
TYPED_KEY_MIN = 16  # a shorter message must fill a quoted argument of the call exactly
TYPED_CHUNK = 32  # rule 9, templates: pieces of this many letters and digits, every 16
TYPED_CHUNKS_MIN = 4  # a text this many pieces long or more may match as a filled-in template
NAMED_FILE_MAX = 256 << 10  # rule 9 reads a file a typing call names only up to this size
TYPING_VERBS = re.compile(r"send-keys|paste-buffer|load-buffer")
TYPING_VERB_BYTES = (b"send-keys", b"paste-buffer", b"load-buffer")
NAMED_PATH = re.compile(r"(?<![\w.~/-])(?:~/|/)[\w.@%+~/-]*\w")
# A script a call runs: a .sh, .bash or .py file, or any file in a bin/ or scripts/ directory.
SCRIPT_PATH = re.compile(r"(?:\.(?:sh|bash|py)|/(?:bin|scripts)/[\w.@%+-]+)$")
SCRIPT_PATH_BYTES = re.compile(rb"(?<![\w.~/-])(?:~/|/)[\w.@%+~/-]*(?:\.(?:sh|bash|py)|/(?:bin|scripts)/[\w.@%+-]+)(?![\w.~/-])")
SCRIPT_HINTS = (b".sh", b".bash", b".py", b"/bin/", b"/scripts/")

MESSAGE_LINE = b'{"type":"message"'
ENTRY_TS = re.compile(rb'"timestamp":"(\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT[\d:.]+Z)"')
SHAKE = re.compile(r"\[shaken ~\d+ tokens — recover: artifact://(\d+) \(region (\d+)\)\]")
AGENT_TYPED = re.compile(r"\[?From the [^\n]{1,100}?:\s|\[(?:From )?Claude\b"
                         r"|[A-Z][A-Z0-9-]{2,}(?: here(?: \(session [0-9a-f]|, at )|, \d\d:\d\dZ\b)")
ESCAPES = re.compile(r"\\+(?:u[0-9a-fA-F]{4}|[nrtbf])")
NOT_ALNUM = re.compile(r"[^a-z0-9]+")
WHITESPACE = re.compile(r"\s+")
DURATION = re.compile(r"(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)([smhd])")
UNITS = {"s": 1, "m": 60, "h": 3600, "d": 86400}


@dataclass
class Session:
    sid: str
    path: Path | None = None
    title: str = ""
    cwd: str = ""


@dataclass
class Message:
    time: datetime
    source: str
    text: str
    session: Session | None = None
    steering: bool = False
    dispatch_id: str | None = None  # the Dispatch message id of a dispatch-turn, or the event's item id
    ref: str | None = None
    context: str | None = None  # what a Dispatch answer or comment replies to
    author: str | None = None  # a dispatch-turn's author, once Dispatch confirms it
    agent_dir: Path | None = None
    history_ids: list[int] = field(default_factory=list)
    beyond: bool = False  # read past --until only to match prompt history and Dispatch messages


@dataclass
class HistoryRow:
    hid: int
    prompt: str
    created: datetime
    cwd: str
    sid: str


@dataclass
class AgentDir:
    root: Path
    history: list[HistoryRow] | None  # None when history.db is missing or unreadable
    by_text: dict[str, list[int]] = field(default_factory=dict)
    rows: dict[int, HistoryRow] = field(default_factory=dict)


def die(msg: str, code: int = 2) -> None:
    print(f"sami-said: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(code)


def warn(msg: str) -> None:
    print(f"sami-said: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)


def parse_when(value: str, now: datetime) -> datetime:
    m = DURATION.fullmatch(value.strip())
    if m:
        return now - timedelta(seconds=float(m.group(1)) * UNITS[m.group(2)])
    text = value.strip().replace("Z", "+00:00").replace("z", "+00:00")
    try:
        t = datetime.fromisoformat(text)
    except ValueError:
        die(f"not a duration or an ISO 8601 time: {value!r}")
    return t.replace(tzinfo=UTC) if t.tzinfo is None else t.astimezone(UTC)


def iso(t: datetime) -> str:
    return t.astimezone(UTC).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def parse_ts(value: str | None) -> datetime | None:
    if not value:
        return None
    try:
        return datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace("Z", "+00:00")).astimezone(UTC)
    except ValueError:
        return None


def norm(text: str) -> str:
    return WHITESPACE.sub(" ", text).strip()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- omp agent directories


def agent_dirs(given: list[str]) -> list[Path]:
    if given:
        return [Path(d).expanduser() for d in given]
    home = Path.home() / ".omp"
    found = [home / "agent"] + sorted(home.glob("profiles/*/agent"))
    return [d for d in found if (d / "sessions").is_dir()]


def load_history(root: Path) -> AgentDir:
    db = root / "history.db"
    ad = AgentDir(root=root, history=None)
    if not db.exists():
        return ad
    try:
        con = sqlite3.connect(f"file:{db}?mode=ro", uri=True, timeout=5)
        try:
            rows = con.execute("select id, prompt, created_at, coalesce(cwd, ''), coalesce(session_id, '') from history").fetchall()
        finally:
            con.close()
    except sqlite3.Error as e:
        warn(f"{db}: {e}; terminal messages from {root} cannot be confirmed and are left out")
        return ad
    ad.history = []
    for hid, prompt, created, cwd, sid in rows:
        row = HistoryRow(hid, prompt, datetime.fromtimestamp(created, UTC), cwd, sid)
        ad.history.append(row)
        ad.rows[hid] = row
        ad.by_text.setdefault(norm(prompt), []).append(hid)
    return ad


def history_match(ad: AgentDir, text: str, sid: str) -> list[int]:
    """Rule 6: the history rows this terminal text was submitted as; empty when it was never typed."""
    exact = ad.by_text.get(norm(text))
    if exact:
        return exact
    t = norm(text)
    hits = []
    for row in ad.history or ():
        if row.sid != sid:
            continue
        h = norm(row.prompt)
        if min(len(h), len(t)) >= FALLBACK_MIN and (h in t or t in h):
            hits.append(row.hid)
    return hits


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- session files


def list_sessions(root: Path) -> list[tuple[Path, float, str]]:
    """Every top-level session file under root/sessions: (path, mtime, session id)."""
    out = []
    try:
        dirs = list(os.scandir(root / "sessions"))
    except OSError:
        return out
    for d in dirs:
        if not d.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False):
            continue
        try:
            files = list(os.scandir(d.path))
        except OSError:
            continue
        for f in files:
            name = f.name
            if not name.endswith(".jsonl") or "_" not in name:
                continue
            try:
                st = f.stat()
            except OSError:
                continue
            out.append((Path(f.path), st.st_mtime, name[name.index("_") + 1 : -len(".jsonl")]))
    return out


SESSION_NAME = re.compile(r"[^_/]+_([0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12})\.jsonl")


def find_nested(root: Path, wanted: set[str], since: float) -> dict[str, Path]:
    """Session files below a top-level session's directory whose session id is in wanted: a
    subagent or lane someone typed into. A file named <time>_<id>.jsonl is matched by its name; any
    other .jsonl only when modified since `since`, by the id in its header."""
    found: dict[str, Path] = {}
    for top in (root / "sessions").iterdir() if (root / "sessions").is_dir() else ():
        if not top.is_dir():
            continue
        for dirpath, _dirs, files in os.walk(top, followlinks=True):  # moved sessions are symlinks
            if dirpath == str(top):
                continue  # the top-level files list_sessions already holds
            for name in files:
                if not name.endswith(".jsonl"):
                    continue
                path = Path(dirpath) / name
                m = SESSION_NAME.fullmatch(name)
                if m:
                    sid = m.group(1)
                else:
                    try:
                        if path.stat().st_mtime < since:
                            continue
                    except OSError:
                        continue
                    sid = read_header(path, "").sid
                if sid in wanted and sid not in found:
                    found[sid] = path
                    if len(found) == len(wanted):
                        return found
    return found


def read_header(path: Path, sid: str) -> Session:
    s = Session(sid=sid, path=path)
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as fh:
            for _ in range(2):
                line = fh.readline()
                if not line:
                    break
                try:
                    e = json.loads(line)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                if e.get("type") == "title" and e.get("title"):
                    s.title = str(e["title"])
                elif e.get("type") == "session":
                    s.sid = str(e.get("id") or sid)
                    s.cwd = str(e.get("cwd") or "")
                    s.title = s.title or str(e.get("title") or "")
    except OSError:
        pass
    return s


def seek_start(fh, size: int, target: str) -> int:
    """A line start before every "message" entry stamped at or after target. Only message entries
    are probed: omp stamps them as it writes them, while a custom_message keeps the time its delivery
    began, and one replayed after a resume sits hours late in the file."""
    lo, hi = 0, size
    while hi - lo > (1 << 20):
        mid = (lo + hi) // 2
        fh.seek(mid)
        fh.readline()
        stamp, pos = None, fh.tell()
        while stamp is None and pos < hi:
            line = fh.readline()
            if not line:
                break
            if line.startswith(MESSAGE_LINE):
                m = ENTRY_TS.search(line, 0, 300)
                stamp = m.group(1).decode() if m else None
            if stamp is None:
                pos = fh.tell()
        if stamp is None or stamp >= target:
            hi = mid
        else:
            lo = pos
    return lo


def shake_regions(path: Path, art: str, cache: dict) -> dict[str, str]:
    key = (path, art)
    if key not in cache:
        regions: dict[str, str] = {}
        log = Path(str(path)[: -len(".jsonl")]) / f"{art}.shake.log"
        if log.exists():
            cur, buf = None, []
            for line in log.read_text(errors="replace").splitlines():
                m = re.match(r"### region (\d+) \(", line)
                if m:
                    if cur is not None:
                        regions[cur] = "\n".join(buf).strip()
                    cur, buf = m.group(1), []
                else:
                    buf.append(line)
            if cur is not None:
                regions[cur] = "\n".join(buf).strip()
        cache[key] = regions
    return cache[key]


def content_text(content) -> str:
    if isinstance(content, str):
        return content
    parts, images = [], 0
    for p in content or ():
        if not isinstance(p, dict):
            continue
        if p.get("type") == "text":
            parts.append(str(p.get("text") or ""))
        elif p.get("type") == "image":
            images += 1
    text = "".join(parts)
    if images and "[Image #" not in text:
        text = (text + " " if text else "") + " ".join("[image]" for _ in range(images))
    return text


def scan_file(path: Path, sid: str, since: datetime, until: datetime, shakes: dict) -> tuple[Session, list[Message]]:
    """Rules 2-5, 7 and 8: the candidates of one session file from since to SEEK_MARGIN past until.
    Those at or after until come back marked `beyond`: they are never printed, but a prompt that
    reached its transcript just after the window is not then shown as one with no transcript copy."""
    session = read_header(path, sid)
    out: list[Message] = []
    try:
        fh = open(path, "rb")
    except OSError:
        return session, out
    with fh:
        size = os.fstat(fh.fileno()).st_size
        start = 0
        if size > SEEK_MIN_BYTES:
            start = seek_start(fh, size, (since - SEEK_MARGIN).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.000Z"))
        fh.seek(start)
        end = until + SEEK_MARGIN
        stop = end.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.000Z").encode()
        for line in fh:
            if line.startswith(MESSAGE_LINE):
                m = ENTRY_TS.search(line, 0, 300)
                if m and m.group(1) > stop:
                    break
            if b'"role":"user"' not in line and b'"customType":"skill-prompt"' not in line:
                continue
            try:
                e = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            t = parse_ts(e.get("timestamp"))
            if t is None or t < since or t >= end:
                continue
            kind = e.get("type")
            if kind == "message":
                m = e.get("message") or {}
                if m.get("role") != "user" or m.get("attribution") not in (None, "user") or m.get("synthetic"):
                    continue
                text = content_text(m.get("content"))
                if "[shaken ~" in text:
                    text = SHAKE.sub(lambda g: shake_regions(path, g.group(1), shakes).get(g.group(2), g.group(0)), text)
                tag = m.get("tag")
            elif kind == "custom_message" and e.get("customType") == "skill-prompt" and e.get("attribution") == "user":
                d = e.get("details") or {}
                if not d.get("name"):
                    continue
                text = f"/skill:{d['name']} {d.get('args') or ''}".strip()
                m, tag = {}, e.get("tag")  # omp puts a Dispatch-typed /skill:'s tag on the entry
            else:
                continue
            tag = tag if isinstance(tag, str) and tag else None
            out.append(Message(time=t, source="dispatch-turn" if tag else "terminal", text=text, session=session,
                               steering=bool(m.get("steering")), dispatch_id=tag, beyond=t >= until))
    return session, out


def agent_typed(text: str) -> bool:
    """Rule T1."""
    return AGENT_TYPED.match(text.lstrip()) is not None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rule 9: agents typing into a pane


@dataclass
class TypingCall:
    time: datetime
    raw: str  # the call's arguments as recorded: JSON text
    key: str  # typing_key of the arguments and of the files they name
    path: Path  # the session file of the agent that made the call


def typing_key(text: str) -> str:
    """Lowercase letters and digits only. A JSON or Python escape (\\n, \\u2011) counts as a gap, so a
    message and the quoted, escaped copy of it in a tool call reduce to the same string."""
    return NOT_ALNUM.sub("", ESCAPES.sub(" ", text).lower())


def recent_jsonl(root: Path, cut: float) -> list[Path]:
    """Every .jsonl below root, nested ones included, modified at or after cut."""
    minutes = int((time.time() - cut) // 60) + 2
    try:
        run = subprocess.run(["find", "-L", str(root), "-name", "*.jsonl", "-type", "f", "-mmin", f"-{minutes}"],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
        if run.returncode == 0 or run.stdout:  # a broken symlink makes find exit 1 after a full listing
            return [Path(p) for p in run.stdout.splitlines()]
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        pass
    found = []
    for dirpath, _dirs, files in os.walk(root, followlinks=True):
        for name in files:
            path = Path(dirpath) / name
            try:
                if name.endswith(".jsonl") and path.stat().st_mtime >= cut:
                    found.append(path)
            except OSError:
                continue
    return found


def named_file(token: str, files: dict[str, str | None]) -> str | None:
    """The text of a small file a tool call names by absolute or ~ path, as it is on disk now."""
    if token not in files:
        files[token] = None
        try:
            path = Path(token).expanduser()
            if path.is_file() and path.stat().st_size <= NAMED_FILE_MAX:
                files[token] = path.read_bytes().decode("utf-8", "replace")
        except (OSError, RuntimeError, ValueError):
            pass
    return files[token]


def script_paths(line: bytes) -> list[bytes]:
    """The script paths in the tool calls of an assistant entry, not in its thinking or text."""
    at = line.find(b'"toolCall"')
    if at < 0 or not any(s in line[at:] for s in SCRIPT_HINTS):
        return []
    return SCRIPT_PATH_BYTES.findall(line, at)


def types_into_pane(text: str | None) -> bool:
    return text is not None and TYPING_VERBS.search(text) is not None


def typing_call(part: dict, t: datetime, path: Path, files: dict[str, str | None]) -> TypingCall | None:
    """A bash or eval tool call that types into a pane: its arguments run send-keys, paste-buffer or
    load-buffer (directly, or through a helper such as tm("send-keys", ...)), or it runs a script
    that does. The text it can type is its arguments and every small file it names: a script that
    builds the text from a template, or a brief sent with send-keys -l "$(cat FILE)" or load-buffer."""
    if part.get("type") != "toolCall" or part.get("name") not in TYPING_TOOLS:
        return None
    raw = json.dumps(part.get("arguments"), ensure_ascii=False)
    types = TYPING_VERBS.search(raw) is not None
    texts = [raw]
    for token in NAMED_PATH.findall(ESCAPES.sub(" ", raw)):
        text = named_file(token, files)
        if text is not None:
            texts.append(text)
            types = types or (SCRIPT_PATH.search(token) is not None and types_into_pane(text))
    return TypingCall(t, raw, typing_key("\n".join(texts)), path) if types else None


def agent_typing_calls(roots: list[Path], start: datetime, end: datetime) -> list[TypingCall]:
    """Rule 9's calls in [start, end), from the session files, nested ones included. The transcript
    store is not used: it cuts a call's arguments at 4000 characters, and the 2026-10-25 wind-down
    cell named send-keys after that."""
    calls: list[TypingCall] = []
    files: dict[str, str | None] = {}
    target = start.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.000Z")
    stop = end.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.000Z").encode()
    names = tuple(f'"name":"{tool}"'.encode() for tool in TYPING_TOOLS)
    for root in roots:
        for path in recent_jsonl(root / "sessions", start.timestamp()):
            try:
                fh = open(path, "rb")
            except OSError:
                continue
            with fh:
                size = os.fstat(fh.fileno()).st_size
                fh.seek(seek_start(fh, size, target) if size > SEEK_MIN_BYTES else 0)
                for line in fh:
                    if not line.startswith(MESSAGE_LINE):
                        continue
                    stamp = ENTRY_TS.search(line, 0, 300)
                    if stamp and stamp.group(1) > stop:
                        break
                    if b'"role":"assistant"' not in line or not any(n in line for n in names):
                        continue
                    if not any(v in line for v in TYPING_VERB_BYTES) and not any(
                            types_into_pane(named_file(p.decode(errors="replace"), files)) for p in set(script_paths(line))):
                        continue
                    try:
                        e = json.loads(line)
                    except ValueError:
                        continue
                    t = parse_ts(e.get("timestamp"))
                    if t is None or t < start:
                        continue
                    for part in (e.get("message") or {}).get("content") or ():
                        call = typing_call(part, t, path, files) if isinstance(part, dict) else None
                        if call is not None:
                            calls.append(call)
    return calls


def typed_by_agent(m: Message, calls: list[TypingCall]) -> bool:
    """Rule 9: another session's typing call held this text shortly before it arrived."""
    key = typing_key(m.text)
    pattern = None
    if len(key) < TYPED_KEY_MIN:
        text = norm(m.text)
        if not text:
            return False
        quoted = re.escape(text)
        pattern = re.compile(rf"(?<=['\"]){quoted}(?=['\"\\])|(?<=-l ){quoted}(?=\s|\\|$)")
    chunks = [key[i:i + TYPED_CHUNK] for i in range(0, len(key) - TYPED_CHUNK + 1, TYPED_CHUNK // 2)]
    for c in calls:
        if not (m.time - TYPED_BEFORE <= c.time <= m.time + TYPED_AFTER):
            continue
        if m.session is not None and m.session.path == c.path:
            continue  # an agent does not type into its own pane: it quoted what it was sent
        if pattern is not None:
            if pattern.search(c.raw):
                return True
        elif key[:TYPED_KEY] in c.key:
            return True  # the start of the text, as typed
        elif len(chunks) >= TYPED_CHUNKS_MIN and sum(ch in c.key for ch in chunks) * 2 >= len(chunks):
            return True  # half of it, as a template with its variables filled in
    return False


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Dispatch


@dataclass
class DispatchConfig:
    url: str
    token: str


def dispatch_config() -> DispatchConfig:
    """The Dispatch server and bearer the dispatch CLI would use: the envoy.json `envoy config-path`
    names, with DISPATCH_URL, DISPATCH_TOKEN_FILE and DISPATCH_TOKEN over it."""
    envoy = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "envoy"
    try:
        path = subprocess.run([str(envoy), "config-path"], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10).stdout.strip()
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        raise RuntimeError(f"cannot find envoy.json: {envoy} config-path failed: {e}") from e
    try:
        cfg = json.loads(Path(path).read_text()).get("dispatch") or {}
    except FileNotFoundError:
        cfg = {}
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{path}: {e}") from e
    if cfg.get("enabled") is False:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{path} sets dispatch.enabled to false")
    url = (os.environ.get("DISPATCH_URL") or cfg.get("serverUrl") or DEFAULT_DISPATCH_URL).rstrip("/")
    token_file = os.environ.get("DISPATCH_TOKEN_FILE")
    if token_file:
        token = Path(token_file).read_text().strip()
    elif os.environ.get("DISPATCH_TOKEN"):
        token = os.environ["DISPATCH_TOKEN"].strip()
    else:
        token = str(cfg.get("token") or "")
        if not token:
            raise RuntimeError(f"no Dispatch token: set dispatch.token in {path}, or DISPATCH_TOKEN or DISPATCH_TOKEN_FILE")
        written_for = urllib.parse.urlsplit((cfg.get("serverUrl") or DEFAULT_DISPATCH_URL).rstrip("/"))
        if urllib.parse.urlsplit(url)[:2] != written_for[:2]:
            raise RuntimeError(f"DISPATCH_URL names {url}, but {path}'s dispatch.token is for another server; set DISPATCH_TOKEN")
        if token.startswith("!"):
            run = subprocess.run(["/bin/sh", "-c", token[1:]], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
            if run.returncode != 0 or not run.stdout.strip():
                raise RuntimeError(f"{path}: the dispatch.token command failed")
            token = run.stdout.strip()
    return DispatchConfig(url=url, token=token)


def api_get(cfg: DispatchConfig, path: str, query: dict | None = None):
    url = cfg.url + path + ("?" + urllib.parse.urlencode(query) if query else "")
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {cfg.token}", "Accept": "application/json"})
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as resp:
        return json.loads(resp.read())


def message_author(cfg: DispatchConfig, mid: str | None, sid: str) -> str | None:
    """Who wrote a Dispatch message: for a turn whose message.created event is before the scanned
    stretch of the log (a delivery replayed hours later, after a resume)."""
    if not mid:
        return None
    try:
        found = api_get(cfg, f"/api/v1/messages/{urllib.parse.quote(mid)}", {"session": sid})
    except (OSError, urllib.error.URLError, ValueError):
        return None
    author = ((found.get("message") or {}).get("author") or {}).get("id") if isinstance(found, dict) else None
    return str(author) if author else None


def open_stream(cfg: DispatchConfig, after: int):
    req = urllib.request.Request(
        f"{cfg.url}/api/v1/events?since={after}",
        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {cfg.token}", "Accept": "text/event-stream"},
    )
    return urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=SSE_IDLE_S)


def stream_events(cfg: DispatchConfig, after: int, head: int | None = None):
    """Events with id > after from the server-sent event log, until it has caught up: a heartbeat,
    or nothing for SSE_IDLE_S seconds, or for SSE_TAIL_S once an event at or past `head` (the newest
    event known when the run started) has arrived, since the catch-up sends its backlog in one burst.
    Other comment lines (`: open`, which newer servers send first) are skipped."""
    resp = open_stream(cfg, after)
    with resp:
        data: list[bytes] = []
        try:
            for raw in resp:
                line = raw.rstrip(b"\r\n")
                if line.startswith(b":"):
                    if line[1:].strip() == b"heartbeat":
                        return
                    continue
                if line.startswith(b"data:"):
                    data.append(line[5:].lstrip())
                elif not line and data:
                    event = json.loads(b"\n".join(data))
                    data = []
                    if head is not None and isinstance(event.get("id"), int) and event["id"] >= head:
                        sock = getattr(getattr(getattr(resp, "fp", None), "raw", None), "_sock", None)
                        if sock is not None:
                            sock.settimeout(SSE_TAIL_S)
                        head = None
                    yield event
        except TimeoutError:
            return


def first_event_after(cfg: DispatchConfig, after: int) -> dict | None:
    for event in stream_events(cfg, after):
        return event
    return None


def recent_event(cfg: DispatchConfig, now: datetime) -> dict | None:
    """An event near the head of the log: the newest event of the most recently updated issue."""
    for lookback in (timedelta(hours=2), timedelta(days=3), timedelta(days=60)):
        found = api_get(cfg, "/api/v1/issues", {"updated_since": iso(now - lookback)})
        issues = found.get("issues", []) if isinstance(found, dict) else found
        if issues:
            newest = max(issues, key=lambda i: i.get("updated_at") or "")
            events = api_get(cfg, f"/api/v1/issues/{urllib.parse.quote(newest['key'])}/events", {"order": "desc", "limit": 1})
            if events:
                return events[0]
    return None


def start_id(cfg: DispatchConfig, target: datetime, now: datetime) -> tuple[int, int | None]:
    """An event id such that the events after it begin at or just before target, and the id of an
    event near the head of the log."""
    anchor = recent_event(cfg, now)
    if anchor is None:
        return 0, None
    head = int(anchor["id"])
    if (parse_ts(anchor.get("created_at")) or now) < target:
        return head, None  # an old anchor: its id says nothing about how much comes after it
    lo, lo_t = 0, None  # the first event after lo is before target
    hi, hi_t = int(anchor["id"]) - 1, parse_ts(anchor.get("created_at"))  # the first event after hi is at or after target
    step = 0
    while hi - lo > 1:
        step += 1
        mid = (lo + hi) // 2
        if lo_t is not None and hi_t is not None and step % 3 and hi_t > lo_t:
            frac = (target - lo_t) / (hi_t - lo_t)
            mid = lo + int(frac * (hi - lo))
            mid = min(max(mid, lo + 1), hi - 1)
        event = first_event_after(cfg, mid)
        t = parse_ts(event.get("created_at")) if event else None
        if t is None or t >= target:
            hi, hi_t = mid, t
        else:
            lo, lo_t = max(mid, int(event["id"]) - 1), t
    return hi, head


def dispatch_rows(cfg: DispatchConfig, user: str, since: datetime, until: datetime, now: datetime):
    """User-authored Dispatch events in [since, until), and every message.created author in it."""
    rows: list[Message] = []
    authors: dict[str, str] = {}
    titles: dict[str, str] = {}  # message id -> the title of the session it was delivered to
    after, head = start_id(cfg, since - DISPATCH_MARGIN, now)
    for e in stream_events(cfg, after, head):
        t = parse_ts(e.get("created_at"))
        if t is None:
            continue
        if t >= until + DISPATCH_MARGIN or t >= now:
            break
        actor = e.get("actor") or {}
        p = e.get("payload") or {}
        if e.get("type") == "message.created":
            a = (p.get("author") or {}).get("id") or actor.get("id")
            if p.get("id") and a:
                authors[str(p["id"])] = str(a)
        elif e.get("type") == "message.delivery" and p.get("message_id") and p.get("title"):
            titles[str(p["message_id"])] = str(p["title"])
        if t < since or t >= until or actor.get("kind") != "user" or actor.get("id") != user:
            continue
        row = dispatch_row(e, t)
        if row is not None:
            rows.append(row)
    for row in rows:
        if row.source == "DISPATCH message" and row.session is not None and not row.session.title:
            row.session.title = titles.get(str(row.dispatch_id), "")
    return rows, authors


def owner_ref(e: dict, p: dict) -> str:
    if e.get("issue_key"):
        return f"dispatch://{e['issue_key']}"
    project = e.get("project") or "?"
    doc = p.get("artifact_name") or p.get("block_artifact") or p.get("artifact_id") or e.get("artifact_id") or "?"
    return f"dispatch://{project}/artifact/{doc}"


def dispatch_row(e: dict, t: datetime) -> Message | None:
    kind, p = e.get("type"), e.get("payload") or {}
    session = None
    if kind == "ask.answered":
        a = p.get("answer") or {}
        picked = [str(s) for s in a.get("selected") or []]
        text = "; ".join(f"[{s}]" for s in picked)
        if a.get("text"):
            text = f"{text} {a['text']}".strip()
        author = p.get("author") or {}
        if author.get("kind") == "session":
            origin = author.get("origin") or {}
            session = Session(sid=str(author.get("id")), title=str(origin.get("session_title") or ""), cwd=str(origin.get("cwd") or ""))
        return Message(t, "DISPATCH answer", text or "(no text)", session, dispatch_id=p.get("id"),
                       ref=f"{owner_ref(e, p)}/ask/{p.get('id')}", context=p.get("question"))
    if kind == "comment.created":
        text = str(p.get("body") or "")
        sug = p.get("suggestion")
        if isinstance(sug, dict) and sug.get("replacement") is not None:
            text = f"{text}\n[suggests: {sug.get('replacement')}]".strip()
        context = None
        if p.get("ask_question"):
            context = f"reply to ask: {p['ask_question']}"
        elif isinstance(p.get("anchor"), dict) and p["anchor"].get("quote"):
            context = f"on: {p['anchor']['quote']}"
        elif p.get("reply_to"):
            context = f"reply to comment {p['reply_to']}"
        return Message(t, "DISPATCH comment", text, None, dispatch_id=p.get("id"),
                       ref=f"{owner_ref(e, p)}/comment/{p.get('id')}", context=context)
    if kind == "message.created":
        target = str(p.get("target") or "")
        if target.startswith("session:"):
            session = Session(sid=target[len("session:"):])
        ref = f"dispatch://{e['issue_key']}/message/{p.get('id')}" if e.get("issue_key") else f"message {p.get('id')} to {target}"
        return Message(t, "DISPATCH message", str(p.get("body") or ""), session, dispatch_id=p.get("id"), ref=ref,
                       context="broadcast" if p.get("broadcast_id") else None)
    if kind in ("artifact.approved", "artifact.changes_requested"):
        label = "DISPATCH approval" if kind == "artifact.approved" else "DISPATCH changes requested"
        return Message(t, label, str(p.get("reason") or "(no reason)"), None,
                       ref=f"{owner_ref(e, p)} {p.get('name') or ''} v{p.get('version') or '?'}".strip())
    return None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- output


def render_text(m: Message, max_chars: int) -> str:
    s = m.session
    head = [iso(m.time), m.source]
    if s is not None:
        head.append(s.sid)
        head.append(s.title or "(untitled)")
        if s.cwd:
            head.append(s.cwd)
    if m.ref:
        head.append(m.ref)
    lines = ["  ".join(head)]
    if m.context:
        lines.append("    (" + cut(norm(m.context), 200) + ")")
    text = cut(m.text, max_chars) if max_chars else m.text
    lines.extend("    " + line for line in text.splitlines() or [""])
    return "\n".join(lines)


def cut(text: str, n: int) -> str:
    return text if len(text) <= n else text[: max(n - 1, 0)] + "…"


def render_json(m: Message, max_chars: int) -> str:
    s = m.session
    obj = {
        "time": iso(m.time),
        "source": m.source,
        "session": s.sid if s else None,
        "title": s.title if s else None,
        "cwd": s.cwd if s else None,
        "text": cut(m.text, max_chars) if max_chars else m.text,
    }
    if max_chars and len(m.text) > max_chars:
        obj["truncated"] = True
    for key in ("steering", "dispatch_id", "ref", "context", "author"):
        value = getattr(m, key)
        if value:
            obj[key] = value
    return json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- main


def main() -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="sami-said", usage=argparse.SUPPRESS, description=__doc__,
                                 formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument("--since", default=DEFAULT_SINCE, help="duration back from now (90m) or ISO time; default 24h")
    ap.add_argument("--until", help="duration back from now or ISO time; default now")
    ap.add_argument("--session", action="append", default=[], help="session id or id prefix; repeatable")
    ap.add_argument("--grep", help="keep messages whose text matches this regex, case-insensitive")
    ap.add_argument("--max-chars", type=int, default=0, help="cut each message to N characters")
    ap.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="one JSON object per line")
    ap.add_argument("--dispatch", action="store_true", help="also list Dispatch answers, comments and messages")
    ap.add_argument("--dispatch-user", default=DEFAULT_DISPATCH_USER, help=f"Dispatch login; default {DEFAULT_DISPATCH_USER}")
    ap.add_argument("--agent-dir", action="append", default=[],
                    help="omp agent directory; default ~/.omp/agent and ~/.omp/profiles/*/agent (with this "
                         "option the transcript store is not asked for rule 9)")
    args = ap.parse_args()
    started = time.monotonic()
    now = datetime.now(UTC)
    since = parse_when(args.since, now)
    until = parse_when(args.until, now) if args.until else now
    if until <= since:
        die("--until must be after --since")
    grep = None
    if args.grep:
        try:
            grep = re.compile(args.grep, re.IGNORECASE)
        except re.error as e:
            die(f"--grep: {e}")

    def wanted(sid: str | None) -> bool:
        return not args.session or (sid is not None and any(sid.startswith(p) for p in args.session))

    typed: list[Message] = []
    sessions: dict[str, Session] = {}
    paths: dict[str, Path] = {}
    stats = {"files": 0, "read": 0, "launch": 0, "agent": 0}
    consumed: set[tuple[Path, int]] = set()  # history rows a transcript message in the window was sent as
    dirs = [load_history(d) for d in agent_dirs(args.agent_dir)]
    shakes: dict = {}

    def take(ad: AgentDir, path: Path, sid: str) -> None:
        stats["read"] += 1
        session, found = scan_file(path, sid, since, until, shakes)
        sessions[session.sid] = session
        for m in found:
            m.agent_dir = ad.root
            if m.source == "terminal":
                if ad.history is None:
                    continue
                m.history_ids = history_match(ad, m.text, session.sid)
                if not m.history_ids:
                    stats["launch"] += not m.beyond
                    continue
                consumed.update((ad.root, h) for h in m.history_ids)
                if agent_typed(m.text):
                    stats["agent"] += not m.beyond
                    continue
            typed.append(m)

    for ad in dirs:
        if ad.history is None:
            warn(f"no readable history.db in {ad.root}: its terminal messages cannot be confirmed and are left out")
        for path, mtime, sid in list_sessions(ad.root):
            stats["files"] += 1
            paths.setdefault(sid, path)
            if mtime >= since.timestamp() and wanted(sid):
                take(ad, path, sid)
        # Rule 1's exception: a session below another one's directory that the prompt history says
        # someone typed into during the window.
        nested = {row.sid for row in ad.history or () if since <= row.created < until and row.sid
                  and row.sid not in paths and wanted(row.sid)}
        for sid, path in find_nested(ad.root, nested, since.timestamp()).items() if nested else ():
            paths[sid] = path
            take(ad, path, sid)

    # Prompt history with no transcript copy in the window.
    for ad in dirs:
        for row in ad.history or ():
            if row.created < since or row.created >= until or (ad.root, row.hid) in consumed or not wanted(row.sid):
                continue
            if agent_typed(row.prompt):
                stats["agent"] += 1
                continue
            draft = norm(row.prompt)
            if any(m.session and m.session.sid == row.sid and m.source == "terminal" and abs(m.time - row.created) <= DRAFT_WINDOW
                   and (norm(m.text).startswith(draft[:DRAFT_PREFIX]) or (len(draft) >= FALLBACK_MIN and draft in norm(m.text)))
                   for m in typed):
                continue
            session = sessions.get(row.sid)
            if session is None:
                session = read_header(paths[row.sid], row.sid) if row.sid in paths else Session(sid=row.sid or "?", cwd=row.cwd)
                sessions[session.sid] = session
            typed.append(Message(time=row.created, source="terminal-history", text=row.prompt, session=session,
                                 agent_dir=ad.root, history_ids=[row.hid]))

    # Rule 9: text an agent typed into the pane with tmux send-keys.
    suspects = [m for m in typed if m.source in ("terminal", "terminal-history") and not m.beyond]
    if suspects:
        calls = agent_typing_calls([ad.root for ad in dirs], min(m.time for m in suspects) - TYPED_BEFORE,
                                   max(m.time for m in suspects) + TYPED_AFTER)
        dropped = {id(m) for m in suspects if typed_by_agent(m, calls)}
        stats["agent"] += len(dropped)
        typed = [m for m in typed if id(m) not in dropped]

    status = 0
    if args.dispatch:
        try:
            cfg = dispatch_config()
            extra, authors = dispatch_rows(cfg, args.dispatch_user, since, until, now)
        except (RuntimeError, OSError, urllib.error.URLError, ValueError) as e:
            warn(f"--dispatch: {e}")
            status = 1
        else:
            turns = set()
            kept = []
            for m in typed:
                if m.source == "dispatch-turn" and not m.beyond:
                    author = authors.get(m.dispatch_id) or message_author(cfg, m.dispatch_id, m.session.sid if m.session else "")
                    if author is None:
                        warn(f"--dispatch: Dispatch did not name the author of message {m.dispatch_id}; it is kept unchecked")
                    elif author != args.dispatch_user:
                        continue
                    m.author = author
                if m.dispatch_id:
                    turns.add(m.dispatch_id)
                kept.append(m)
            typed = kept
            for m in extra:
                if m.source == "DISPATCH message" and m.dispatch_id in turns:
                    continue  # already shown as the dispatch-turn it became
                if m.session is not None:
                    known = sessions.get(m.session.sid)
                    if known is None and m.session.sid in paths:
                        known = read_header(paths[m.session.sid], m.session.sid)
                    if known is not None:
                        m.session = Session(sid=known.sid, path=known.path, title=known.title or m.session.title,
                                            cwd=known.cwd or m.session.cwd)
                if args.session and not wanted(m.session.sid if m.session else None):
                    continue
                typed.append(m)

    typed = [m for m in typed if not m.beyond]
    if grep is not None:
        typed = [m for m in typed if grep.search(m.text)]
    typed.sort(key=lambda m: m.time)
    out = sys.stdout
    for i, m in enumerate(typed):
        if args.json:
            out.write(render_json(m, args.max_chars) + "\n")
        else:
            out.write(("\n" if i else "") + render_text(m, args.max_chars) + "\n")
    counts: dict[str, int] = {}
    for m in typed:
        counts[m.source] = counts.get(m.source, 0) + 1
    summary = ", ".join(f"{n} {k}" for k, n in sorted(counts.items())) or "none"
    warn(f"{len(typed)} messages ({summary}) from {iso(since)} to {iso(until)}; read {stats['read']} of {stats['files']} session "
         f"files in {time.monotonic() - started:.1f}s; left out {stats['launch']} prompts never typed in a terminal and "
         f"{stats['agent']} texts agents typed")
    return status


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main())
    except BrokenPipeError:
        sys.exit(0)
